# Line-ending policy. Added when a Windows workstation joined the project.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. That is harmless for most source but breaks three things here, so
# they are pinned explicitly rather than left to a global setting that varies
# per machine.
#
# Deliberately NOT using `* text=auto`: every file in this repo is already
# stored LF, and a blanket rule would renormalize all 562 of them.

# ── must stay LF ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A shell script with CRLF fails under Git Bash and in the Linux worker
# container with "\r: command not found" or "bad interpreter" — and the
# container entrypoint failing is the silent-Forge failure mode all over again.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf

# ── byte-stable data: never convert ──────────────────────────────────────
# The results/study corpus and the Forge decklists are compared, hashed and
# parsed byte-wise. CRLF would inflate them and break byte-exact checks.
*.jsonl         -text
*.json          -text
*.dck           -text

# ── binary ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The pip/mascot WebPs are reproduced byte-for-byte by
# Design System/tools/export_pips.py; any conversion would break that check.
*.webp          binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jar           binary
*.docx          binary
*.zip           binary
*.db            binary
